Open Image Denoise 2.4.1 on powerpc64le.

OIDN's CPU device is ISPC kernels plus a small amount of C++; the only
architecture knowledge is the OIDN_ARCH selector (X64 / ARM64) that picks
ispc targets, the --arch value, and the per-ISA kernel blocking constants.
Add PPC64LE alongside ARM64 using ispc's VSX targets (>= 1.31,
PPC64_ENABLED): vsx-i32x8 for the f32 kernels, vsx-i32x8 / vsx-i16x16 for
the f16 ones (the same widths as NEON, so the same 32-byte channel block),
the NEON convolution blocking constants, a CPUArch::VSX value so the device
enumerates instead of reporting "Unknown" and registering nothing, and
--arch=ppc64le.  The x86-only pieces (cpuid, AMX, DNNL) are already gated
behind OIDN_ARCH_X64 and are untouched.

One link-time consequence: ispc lowers float16 on the VSX targets through
LLVM's soft-float helpers (__extendhfsf2, __truncsfhf2, ...), which libgcc
does not provide on POWER (GCC has no _Float16 there).  The device module
then links fine but fails dlopen(RTLD_NOW) and OIDN enumerates no CPU
device at all.  The PPC64LE branch links compiler-rt's builtins archive
into the module (override with -DOIDN_PPC64LE_RT_BUILTINS=<path>).  The f16
kernels are only selected on the AMX path, so on VSX they are dead code
that merely has to resolve.

Portability fix, worth sending upstream (github.com/RenderKit/oidn).
diff -ruN a/cmake/oidn_ispc.cmake b/cmake/oidn_ispc.cmake
--- a/cmake/oidn_ispc.cmake	2026-09-10 17:05:49.558552796 -0600
+++ b/cmake/oidn_ispc.cmake	2026-09-10 18:26:56.490290081 -0600
@@ -92,6 +92,8 @@
 
   if(OIDN_ARCH STREQUAL "X64")
     set(ISPC_ARCHITECTURE "x86-64")
+  elseif(OIDN_ARCH STREQUAL "PPC64LE")
+    set(ISPC_ARCHITECTURE "ppc64le")
   elseif(OIDN_ARCH STREQUAL "ARM64")
     set(ISPC_ARCHITECTURE "aarch64")
     if(APPLE AND ISPC_VERSION VERSION_LESS "1.16.0")
diff -ruN a/cmake/oidn_platform.cmake b/cmake/oidn_platform.cmake
--- a/cmake/oidn_platform.cmake	2026-09-10 17:05:49.558552796 -0600
+++ b/cmake/oidn_platform.cmake	2026-09-10 18:26:56.489947188 -0600
@@ -9,6 +9,8 @@
 endif()
 if(${CMAKE_SYSTEM_PROCESSOR} MATCHES "arm64|aarch64|ARM64" OR IOS)
   set(OIDN_ARCH "ARM64")
+elseif(${CMAKE_SYSTEM_PROCESSOR} MATCHES "ppc64le|powerpc64le")
+  set(OIDN_ARCH "PPC64LE")
 else()
   set(OIDN_ARCH "X64")
 endif()
diff -ruN a/common/platform.cpp b/common/platform.cpp
--- a/common/platform.cpp	2026-09-10 17:05:49.559034573 -0600
+++ b/common/platform.cpp	2026-09-10 18:26:56.492224852 -0600
@@ -85,6 +85,8 @@
     name += " (x86-64)";
